# Normalise to LF in the repository *and* in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Plain `text=auto` checks out CRLF on Windows, which makes `gofmt -l` flag every
# file locally while CI (Linux, LF) sees nothing wrong — a difference that costs
# more than it saves. Shell scripts and Makefiles also break outright with CRLF
# once they reach a container.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary corpus material must never be touched.
*.pdf  binary
*.docx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary
